# Hex literals — the C lexer delegates numbers to strtod, which accepts
# 0x/0X hex integers, hex fractions (digits a-f in the fraction!), and the
# binary exponent p/P. `0x` with no hex digit lexes as `0` then an ident,
# so only real hex prefixes take this path. Byte-for-byte parity case for
# ouroboros#57 item 1 (was: `0x10` lexed as `0` + stray `x10`).
print of 0x10
print of 0X10
print of 0xff
print of 0xFF
print of 0xABCDEF
h is 0x1A
print of h
print of (h + 0x1)
# hex float forms strtod accepts
print of 0x1p3
print of 0x.8
print of 0x10.f
# arithmetic on hex, precedence unchanged
print of (0x10 * 2 + 0x2)
